As so often with NetHack, the answer is not simply "yes" or "no". :)
If you are a gnome or a dwarf, it can be much easier because the gnomes
and dwarves in the mines will be peaceful. Depending on your character,
you might want to go there anyway, though - Minetown has shops and an
altar, both of which are helpful to most games.

You might want to stop at Minetown, though - the deeper levels can have
polymorph traps, so it can be dangerous there without magic resistance
or polymorph control. (There is more to this than just "below Minetown",
but it's a typical rule of thumb.)

If you already have magic resistance - for example, as wizard from your
starting cloak of magic resistance -, you might want to go deeper in
the mines to find the luckstone and possibly some spellbooks or potions.

However, the monsters to fight in the mines can indeed be strong,
especially for a wizard. It should be survivable using Elbereth, though.

